<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's BFE resumes trade.</title>
<headline>Portugal's BFE resumes trade.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Suspension of trade in Portuguese bank Banco de Fomento e Exterior on Lisbon bourse was lifted at 1100 GMT, the bourse said.</p>
<p>The shares had been interrupted by the arrival of formal documents relating to the already completed purchase of the bank by Banco Portugues de Investimento, market sources said.</p>
<p>BPI bought BFE from the state for $900 million last month.</p>
<p>BFE closed on the Lisbon bourse on Monday at 2,556 escudos.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
